In practice, you only need to use the non-parameteric prior when you have a very large deviation from the parametric prior. In most cases, the results are nearly identical within a 1-2% difference in the expression values. 

In your case, I would recommend just trying it and seeing if it makes a difference. If it does, trust the non-parametric.

Evan


